<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57599" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κισσύβιον</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], τό</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rustic drinking-cup</i> of wood, used by the Cyclops,
				<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.346
			</span></i>; by Eumaeus, <i><span class="en">
				14.78
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἀμφῶες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					1.27
				</span></i>
			 (but expld. as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόνωτον
			ποτήριον</span>, Philem.Gloss. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				11.476f
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλίγῳ ἥδετο κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Aet.</u>
					1.1.12
				</span></i>
			.—So called, either as made of ivy-wood, Eumolp. ap.
				<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				11.477a
			</span></i>; or because adorned with ivy-wreaths, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				6.97
			</span></i>: in late Prose, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴνου κ.</span>
				Prisc.<i><span class="en">
				p.316
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i></div>
